        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The ledger service was experiencing high latency (p99 = 3400ms, SLO = 300ms).\n- Logs indicated excessive GC pauses (up to 1.9s) and that only 3 replicas were running, despite a capacity plan calling for at least 6 (8 recommended) during high load.\n- The GC pause metric confirmed sustained high pauses, and the replica count was below the recommended level.\n\nRemediation:\n- I scaled the ledger-service from 3 to 8 replicas to match the expected load.\n- Posted a public status update to inform customers of the mitigation.\n- Latency has since dropped back within SLO (now 240ms p99).\n\nSummary: The issue was caused by under-provisioning during a high-load period, leading to GC pressure and high latency. Scaling up the service resolved the problem.",
